cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Wildfire Watch (Sentinel Api): Real-Time Indonesia VIIRS Hotspot & Stationary Industrial Thermal Separation"
message: "If you use this software or methodology in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Fajrianshah"
    given-names: "Evans Azka"
    affiliation: "National Research and Innovation Agency (BRIN); Graduate School, Universitas Gadjah Mada"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-24"
license: MIT
url: "https://fire.transbulent.id"
repository-code: "https://github.com/gisrad/wildfire-watch"
abstract: >-
  Real-time webGIS platform and edge ingestion pipeline for monitoring NASA FIRMS VIIRS 375 m (NOAA-20 and NOAA-21) active fire detections across the Indonesian archipelago. Implements a two-tier stationary thermal filter that flags suspected coal-fired power plants (PLTU), metallurgical smelters, upstream oil and gas flares, cement/pulp kilns, and active volcano craters, separately from candidate vegetation and peatland wildfires (karhutla), while preserving peatland hydrological corridor alerts. Source categories are suspicions, not confirmed attribution.
